dici, advocati) replaced orators (oratores) during the Roman Dominate period. Leo I (460 CE) demanded some lawyers produce a certificate proving their professional instruction, a requirement which was later demanded in the provinces. '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 865, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 771})
