lier efforts towards the professionalization of the Russian civil service under Alexander I and the establishment of law faculties in urban centers, leading to a cadre of Russian jurists in administrative, judicial, and academic roles\u200b\u200b.\r\nThe reforms initiated under Alexander II in 1864 marked a significant shift, creating a more formal and professional legal environment and contributing to the evolution towards a constitutional monarchy by 1906\u200b\u200b.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 886, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 788})
